# An animated Mutavault is a 2/2 creature, so 3 damage from Bot2's Lightning Bolt is lethal damage (CR 704.5g) and the
# land card goes to its owner's graveyard. While the animation is on the stack it is only a land, which "any target"
# (CR 115.4) does not include, so the Bolt is refused then and cast once the animation has resolved. Bot1 animates it
# on turn 3 with a Swamp; Bot2 answers with a Mountain.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mutavault
Swamp
Swamp x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mutavault.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault.Activate(Ability: {1})
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Pass
! Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Mutavault
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
